# Living Survey: Quantum_Computing                                                                             
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
## Introduction                                                                                                
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
This document collects the scientific literature regarding **Quantum_Computing**.                              
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
## Quantum Hardware and Architectures                                                                          
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
Recent research continues to explore novel computational paradigms beyond traditional transistor and qubit     
systems. A unified framework redefining matter and particle behavior proposes atom computing as a deterministic
alternative, utilizing controlled flows of single electrons or photons to overcome material scaling            
constraints[^10.34257_gjsfra257362]. Furthermore, comparative studies provide standardized architectural models
for digital, quantum, and biological computers, highlighting the immense performance potential of quantum      
systems while establishing baseline engineering descriptions[^10.1109_mc.2021.3083430].                        
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
## Quantum Software, Toolchains, and Simulation                                                                
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
The ecosystem surrounding quantum software development is maturing, with empirical analyses of developer       
communities revealing that hybrid quantum-classical computing and circuit implementation dominate practitioner 
discussions, alongside tools like Qiskit and Q-sharp[^https:__openalex.org_W7155247427]. To support research,  
open-source frameworks like PULSEE have been developed to simulate extensive magnetic resonance observables and
quantum gate time-evolutions, bridging quantum information science with condensed matter                       
physics[^10.1016_j.cpc.2022.108598]. Additionally, hybrid quantum-classical granular computing approaches are  
being introduced to optimize continuous search spaces, statistically enhancing evolutionary algorithms on      
limited-qubit processors[^10.1007_s41066-022-00348-9].                                                         
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
## Quantum Communication and Cryptography                                                                      
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
Secure quantum communication remains a pivotal area of investigation. Practical implementations of the BB84    
quantum key distribution (QKD) protocol have been simulated in Python, modeling state preparation,             
eavesdropping attacks, and classical post-processing to demonstrate provably secure                            
communication[^10.6084_m9.figshare.32051724]. Broader overviews of quantum cryptography detail foundational    
protocols (BB84, B92, B91) and analyze vulnerabilities such as photon splitting and faked-state attacks,       
alongside the implications of Shor's algorithm[^https:__openalex.org_W7112574406]. The theoretical foundation  
for a global quantum Internet is also being established, outlining protocols for ultra-secure connectivity and 
large-scale quantum device networks[^10.31695_ijerat.2025.9.1]. Concurrently, the cryptographic landscape is   
adapting to quantum threats; recent cryptanalysis on Learning With Errors (LWE) problems demonstrates improved 
dual lattice attacks that significantly reduce the security margins of NIST post-quantum cryptography finalists
like Kyber and Dilithium[^10.5281_zenodo.6493704]. In response, advanced hybrid encryption systems             
incorporating post-quantum considerations and benchmarking against quantum algorithms like Grover's and Shor's 
are being developed[^10.56975_tijer.v13i3.161368].                                                             
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
## Quantum Applications in Science and Industry                                                                
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
Quantum computing is increasingly applied to complex scientific and industrial problems. In computational fluid
dynamics (CFD), quantum algorithms based on Navier-Stokes equations and the Lattice Boltzmann Method are being 
reviewed and implemented to simulate aeronautical heat exchangers and 2D fluid flows[^10.11159_icffts23.133]   
[^10.21741_9781644902813-38]. In materials science, practical guides for quantum annealing enable the          
configurational analysis of defective structures, such as graphene, translating chemical models into qubit     
representations for energy calculations[^10.1063_5.0151346]. Finally, tracking emerging technological trends   
through open repositories and financial news provides valuable insights into the industrial adoption trajectory
of quantum technologies[^10.1007_978-3-031-90727-2_20].                                                        
                                                                                                               

